<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  SeanDexCo — עברית

  Note on the directory name: Android resolves Hebrew under the legacy "iw"
  code, which is why MainActivity already calls setDirection(new Locale("iw")).
  An identical copy lives in values-he for newer resolution paths.

  RTL is already enabled app-wide (android:supportsRtl="true"), so layouts
  mirror automatically. Glucose numerals stay LTR — digits read left-to-right
  even in Hebrew text, and mg/dL is a unit, not a word to translate.
-->
